Array in Javascript

-> Arrays are Object in JS 

-> Java array & javascript array comparision

Aspect |                Java                        |     Javascript
_____________________________________________________________________________
Size   |           Fixed                            | Dynamic grow & shrink automatically
Typing |  Strict homogeneious                       | Hetero any data can be added including number, boolean,string, objects
Memory |  Contigious block on heap                  | Object -like paced or dictonory 
Defaults |   0, null, false                         |  Empty read as undefined
Resize |  Allocate new,copy ,replace                | Automatic, amortized O(1) push
Best for | Fixed values else use collection         | any data objects,API data, text fixtures

-> An array is just an object with numeric keys plus a length property. [typeof array is object]

Various declaration ways:
const marks = [78, 84, 91, 66, 72];   // literal (preferred)
const empty = [];                     // empty, grow later
const demo1 = new Array(5);           // length 5, sparse
const demo2 = Array.of(5);            // [5]
const demo3 = Array.from("hello");    // ['h','e','l','l','o']


EX: const profile = ["Jatin", 32, true, { role: "SDET" }, [10, 20, 30]];

How to store on memory ?

Refernce veariable will be stored on stack holding the address of actual array objec on heap location 
which is a contiguous block with a length field followed by the element slots

For int[] arr = { 10, 20, 30 };
STACK MEMORY HEAP MEMORY
+------------------+ +---------------------------------+
| arr --> 1000 | ------------> | addr 1000: |
                               | length = 3 |
                               | [0] = 10 |
                               | [1] = 20 |
                               | [2] = 30 |
                           +---------------------------
-->  Elements sit next to each other in memory, hardware-friendly
--> To know the type of object if array ---- Array.isArray()




